---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "./header.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <Header />

  <main class="content-page">
    <div class="content-container">
      <header class="page-intro">
        <h1>Methods</h1>
        <p>[Overview - recommend HNC definition here]</p>
      </header>

      <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="method-1">
        <h2 id="method-1">Data</h2>

        <div class="content-row">
          <div class="content-primary">
            <h3>Population</h3>
            <p>
              Information on patients diagnosed with primary malignant HNC
              cancer in England from 1 January 2016 to 31 December 2021 from
              National Cancer Registration Dataset (NCRD)<sup
                ><a href="#ref-1" aria-label="1">1</a></sup
              > and from 1 January 2022 - 31 December 2023 from the Rapid Cancer Registration
              Database (RCRD)<sup><a href="#ref-2" aria-label="2">2</a></sup>.
            </p>
            <h3>Access</h3>
            <p>
              The NHS England Secure Data Environment (SDE)<sup
                ><a href="#ref-3" aria-label="3">3</a></sup
              > was used to access the cancer data. In line with the SDE disclosure
              policy<sup><a href="#ref-4" aria-label="4">4</a></sup>, counts are
              rounded to the nearest five and those below 10 are suppressed.
              Analyses were carried out in STATA version 18<sup
                ><a href="#ref-5" aria-label="5">5</a></sup
              >.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="content-secondary" aria-label="Additional information">
            <h3>[Optional additional detail]</h3>
            <p>[Placeholder]</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="method-2">
        <h2 id="method-2">Approach</h2>

        <div class="content-row">
          <div class="content-primary">
            <h3>Incidence</h3>
            <p>
              Incidence rates per 100,000 person-years were derived using Office
              for National Statistics (ONS) mid-year population estimates<sup
                ><a href="#ref-6" aria-label="6">6</a></sup
              > for the years 2016-2022 by age, sex and Lower-level Super Output Area
              (LSOA). Incidence for 2023 was derived using 2022 population denominators.
            </p>
            <h3>Survival</h3>
            <p>
              Estimates of one- and five-year net survival estimates were
              derived using the most up-to-date methodology<sup
                ><a href="#ref-7" aria-label="7">7</a></sup
              >.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="content-secondary" aria-label="Additional information">
            <h3>[Optional additional detail]</h3>
            <p>[Placeholder]</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="method-3">
        <h2 id="method-3">Covariables</h2>

        <div class="content-row">
          <div class="content-primary">
            <h3>Deprivation</h3>
            <p>
              Patients' deprivation was classified according to quintiles of
              Index of Multiple Deprivation 2019<sup
                ><a href="#ref-8" aria-label="8">8</a></sup
              > at LSOA level.
            </p>
            <h3>Region</h3>
            <p>Government Office Region of residence at cancer diagnosis.</p>
            <h3>Stage</h3>
            <p>
              Information on how advanced the cancer was at diagnosis was
              recorded in the NCRD<sup
                ><a href="#ref-1" aria-label="1">1</a></sup
              > for diagnoses up to 2021. Stage was unavailable for 2022-2023. Tumours
              were grouped into early (TNM I and II), advanced (III and IV), or unknown<sup
                ><a href="#ref-9" aria-label="9">9</a></sup
              >.
            </p>
            <h3>Route to diagnosis</h3>
            <p>
              The pathway taken by patients through the health service to cancer
              diagnosis was available for NCRD<sup
                ><a href="#ref-1" aria-label="1">1</a></sup
              > data up to 2018. The RCRD<sup
                ><a href="#ref-2" aria-label="2">2</a></sup
              > includes unvalidated estimates for 2022-2023. Patient pathways were
              categorised into Emergency or Non-Emergency routes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <aside class="img-secondary" aria-label="Additional information">
            <img
              src="/HNCancer/images/English_regions.svg.png"
              style="width: 100%; max-width: 500px;"
              alt="Map showing the nine English regions"
            />
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="references" aria-labelledby="references-title">
        <h2 id="references-title">References</h2>
        <ol>
          <li id="ref-1">
            Henson KE, Elliss-Brookes L, Coupland VH, et al. Data Resource
            Profile: National Cancer Registration Dataset in England.
            <em>International Journal of Epidemiology</em>. 2019;49(1):16–16h.
            doi: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/ije/dyz076"
              >10.1093/ije/dyz076</a
            >.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-2">
            National Disease Registration Service. <em
              >Rapid registration QA report (CAS2609)</em
            >. NHS England; 2025.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-3">
            NHS England. <em>Secure Data Environment service</em> [Internet]. 2025.
            Available from:
            <a
              href="https://digital.nhs.uk/services/secure-data-environment-service"
              >Secure Data Environment service</a
            >.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-4">
            NHS England. <em>Output your results</em>. Available from:
            <a
              href="https://digital.nhs.uk/services/secure-data-environment-service/access-and-support-for-the-secure-data-environment/user-guides/output-your-results"
              >Output your results: Secure Data Environment user guide</a
            >.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-5">
            StataCorp. <em>Stata Statistical Software: Release 18</em>. College
            Station, TX: StataCorp LLC; 2023.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-6">
            Office for National Statistics. <em
              >Lower layer Super Output Area population estimates</em
            >. Available from:
            <a
              href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/populationestimates/datasets/lowersuperoutputareamidyearpopulationestimates"
              >Lower layer Super Output Area mid-year population estimates</a
            >.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-7">
            Perme MP, Stare J, Estève J. On estimation in relative survival.
            <em>Biometrics</em>. 2012 Mar;68(1):113-120. doi: <a
              href="https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1541-0420.2011.01640.x"
              >10.1111/j.1541-0420.2011.01640.x</a
            >.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-8">
            Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government.
            <em>English Indices of Deprivation 2019</em>. 2019. Available from:
            <a
              href="https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/english-indices-of-deprivation-2019"
              >English Indices of Deprivation 2019</a
            >.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-9">
            Edge SB, et al., editors. <em>AJCC Cancer Staging Manual</em>. 7th
            ed. Springer; 2010. Used for tumours diagnosed in 2016-2018. TNM
            Classification of Malignant Tumours. 8th ed. UICC; 2017. Used for
            tumours diagnosed from 2018 onwards.
          </li>

          <li id="ref-10">
            Elliss-Brookes L, McPhail S, Ives A, et al. Routes to diagnosis for
            cancer - determining the patient journey using multiple routine data
            sets. <em>British Journal of Cancer</em>. 2012;107:1220-1226. doi: <a
              href="https://doi.org/10.1038/bjc.2012.408"
              >10.1038/bjc.2012.408</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  img {
    display: block;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
</style>
